Allen Linux 5.10.274 source checkpoint
====================================

Target: Huawei Mate 60 Pro, ALN-AL00 / HWALN, Kirin 9000S.
Date: 2026-11-20.

This tree starts from the device's published Linux 5.10.43 sources and carries
the ordered stable updates through Linux 5.10.274, together with the Android
and hardware adaptations needed by this device. It is still an OEM Android
kernel. Android common parity, OEM/core separation, and a stable GKI/KMI are
unfinished.

Configuration
-------------

There is one source tree and two ARM64 configurations:

  arch/arm64/configs/allen_secure_defconfig
    Based on the accepted #101 configuration. Mandatory module signatures,
    Huawei root checks/scanning, and SELinux enforcing remain enabled.

  arch/arm64/configs/allen_relaxed_defconfig
    Based on the accepted #103 local debug configuration. Module signatures
    are generated but are not mandatory. Huawei PROC_CHECK_ROOT and
    HW_ROOT_SCAN are disabled. SELinux remains present and starts Enforcing
    through the built-in enforcing=1 argument. Magisk root can explicitly
    change its mode after boot with setenforce; no permissive startup or
    automatic mode-changing service is installed by this tree.

Both retain ThinLTO, enforcing CFI, BTI/BHB, PRMEM/HKIP, and the same hardware
configuration. The relaxed configuration lowers protection for local testing;
it does not turn off every kernel hardening feature.

These defconfigs are Kbuild savedefconfig output, not copies of an entire
workspace or separate source versions. Their regenerated effective settings
match #101 and #103 respectively, with one packaging change: the existing
public trust certificate now lives at certs/allen-stock-module-signing.pem
instead of an external ../../configs path. Its contents are unchanged.

Build
-----

Use x86_64 Linux and Android Clang/LLD 12.0.7, revision clang-r416183b1
(Android build 7485623). Required host tools include make, bash, Python 3,
GCC/G++ for host tools, bc, flex, bison, pkg-config, OpenSSL development
headers/libraries, libelf development headers/libraries, and standard Unix
utilities. The saved cross prefixes are aarch64-linux-gnu- and
arm-linux-gnueabi-; LLVM and its integrated assembler compile the target code.

From the extracted kernel root, set the compiler location and a separate
output directory. The function keeps the validated build arguments together:

  export ALLEN_CLANG=/absolute/path/to/clang-r416183b1
  export ALLEN_OUT="$PWD/../out-allen"
  export PATH="$ALLEN_CLANG/bin:$PATH"
  mkdir -p "$ALLEN_OUT"
  make_allen() {
      make ARCH=arm64 O="$ALLEN_OUT" LLVM=1 LLVM_IAS=1 \
          CROSS_COMPILE=aarch64-linux-gnu- \
          CROSS_COMPILE_COMPAT=arm-linux-gnueabi- \
          CLANG_PREBUILTS_PATH="$ALLEN_CLANG/" LOCALVERSION= \
          LD="$ALLEN_CLANG/bin/ld.lld --thinlto-jobs=2 --thinlto-cache-policy=cache_size_bytes=1g" \
          "$@"
  }

Select exactly one configuration:

  make_allen allen_secure_defconfig

or, for the debug profile:

  make_allen allen_relaxed_defconfig

Then build the kernel and matching modules together:

  make_allen olddefconfig
  make_allen -j8 Image modules

The outputs are in the separate output directory:

  arch/arm64/boot/Image
  drivers/platform_drivers/modem/modem_driver.ko

Kbuild generates a new local signing key under the output directory's certs/
when one has not been supplied. No private signing key is distributed in this
source archive. Keep that generated key private. Before deploying a module,
strip it as appropriate and sign it with scripts/sign-file from the same
build and the corresponding local key. Match kernel/module symbol versions
and vermagic; do not mix an old stock module with a newly built kernel.

The device has a boot partition and a separate Magisk ramdisk partition.
Source compilation does not create an OEM-signed boot image. Integration
requires the device's original DTB, boot header/stub, runtime firmware and
matching module filesystem, which are not distributed in this source archive.

Checkpoint and limits
---------------------

The secure #101 and relaxed #103 builds both reached normal Android and
automatically loaded their matching signed modem module. On #103, startup was
Enforcing, sig_enforce was N, and a Magisk setenforce 0 / setenforce 1 round
trip succeeded. The device was left Enforcing. CE storage, essential services,
partition/module readbacks, PRMEM and zero WARN/Oops counters were checked;
the independent ramdisk was unchanged.

The configuration/profile packaging step did not change runtime C/assembly
code. It validates defconfig regeneration and extraction separately; it does
not repeat or extend the earlier hardware acceptance. Full hardware, network,
power, performance, OEM firmware parity, and GKI/KMI certification remain open.
Future builds use new keys/timestamps and are not promised byte-identical to
the installed test images.

Archive contents and licensing
-----------------------------

COPYING, LICENSES/, source copyrights, and the upstream documentation remain
in place. No new blanket license replaces the individual file licenses.
SOURCE_INFO.json records the exact source revision, kernel tree and archive
filters. SHA256SUMS records each included file's content.

The archive omits five unused OEM prebuilt ELF host tools and ten unselected
Mali firmware .wa blobs, plus the zero-byte stock -c import artifact. These
paths are listed in SOURCE_INFO.json. Formal source, Kbuild scripts, debug
features, KUnit log fixtures and the reproducible upstream perf PE test data
are retained. The archive contains no workspace .git, output/cache directory,
device log, flashed image, external compiler, or private signing key.
